    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Input and Validation\nThe workflow starts with a POST Webhook that receives an array of prompts.\n\nNormalize Request extracts the required fields.\n\nExpand & Enrich Prompts converts the array into separate n8n items, generates IDs, calculates prompt length, and adds validation metadata.\n\nKeep Valid Prompts removes empty or very short prompts before processing.",
        "height": 432,
        "width": 256
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -64,
        144
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "id": "f1377a43-5cb2-43a4-8196-e8406cc75cd0",
      "name": "Sticky Note"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Loop and External API\nProcess Prompts One by One loops through the valid prompts with a batch size of 1.\n\nSearch Wikipedia calls a real public API using the topic of each prompt.\n\nBuild Agent Input combines the original prompt with relevant Wikipedia context and prepares a structured input for the custom agent.",
        "height": 368,
        "width": 256
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        560,
        176
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "id": "8335b973-2f72-4e50-9bbd-f6c2a31f1238",
      "name": "Sticky Note1"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Custom Prompt Doctor Agent\nThis custom n8n node improves prompts using the Gemini API.\n\nThe agent follows an iterative loop:\n\nExecutor → Judge → Score Check → Reviser\n\nIt repeats until the score threshold is reached or the maximum number of iterations is completed.\n\nThe Gemini API key is stored securely in n8n Credentials and is not hardcoded.",
        "height": 416,
        "width": 256
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1408,
        -416
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "id": "14720133-b2de-4f65-8969-4405fd103497",
      "name": "Sticky Note2"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Routing, Error Handling and Output\nRoute Agent Result uses a Switch node to classify each result as Approved, Needs Review, or Error.\n\nEach branch adds a clear status before the results are combined using the Merge node.\n\nWikipedia and Prompt Doctor errors continue through a handled fallback path.\n\nAfter all items finish processing, Respond to Webhook returns the final JSON response to the caller.",
        "height": 512,
        "width": 256
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1728,
        -544
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "id": "acb7560d-08e0-49e8-872e-21c349242f7a",
      "name": "Sticky Note3"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Workflow Output\nThe final response contains the original prompt, improved prompt, s core, convergence status, iteration count, and any handled error message.",
        "height": 192,
        "width": 256
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1008,
        -288
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "id": "6aa95878-dc24-4c07-be89-baf5ac26055b",
      "name": "Sticky Note4"
    }
  ],
